			<div class="content" id="post-content-1758346">
									

<p>I actually like the article without the clear association with the Greek underworld. A tree that uses a psychic vector to spread its &quot;seeds&quot; is unexpected and quirky enough for me to instantly love it, and after that the references to the Classical underworld seemed tacked-on and less interesting. It's possible that I might be missing something because of my merely passing familiarity with Greek mythology.</p>
<p>Also, a nitpicky question. Why did they attack the plant with herbicides? It seems like axes or fire would be a lot faster and more decisive. If I were dealing with an out-of-control plant, I think I'd rather have a chainsaw or a gallon of gasoline on hand than a spray bottle of Roundup. It didn't affect my appreciation of the article at all, it's just something that made me go &quot;huh?&quot;</p>
<p>I still liked it a lot, +1.</p>

							</div>

								
